---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectLinks from '../components/ProjectLinks.astro';
import { getPhase } from '../data/phases';

const financeColor = getPhase('finance').color;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Domains - projecttrack.dev"
  description="A data science career has two axes: domain and function. See where the track's projects fit."
>
  <article class="domains">
    <p class="eyebrow">Domains</p>
    <h1>Choose your lane</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      A data science career has two axes. <strong>Domain</strong> is where your data lives: finance, health, retail,
      sports. <strong>Function</strong> is what you do to it: analyst, ML engineer, researcher. A role is one point
      on each axis, not just a domain.
    </p>

    <section class="finance-lane" style={`--lane-color: ${financeColor};`}>
      <p class="lane-label">The deep lane</p>
      <h2>Finance</h2>
      <p>
        <ProjectLinks orders={[8, 9, 10, 11]} /> are the finance lane of the main track: market forecasting, credit
        risk, a data pipeline, and a document assistant built on filings. This is the domain the site teaches to
        depth, including how to break into it. See <a href="/about/">About</a> for the CFA angle and the
        <a href="/recruiting/">Recruiting Timeline</a> for application windows.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="domain-grid">
      <div class="domain-card">
        <h3>Health</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Chest X-ray classification</li>
          <li>Predicting lung-function decline from CT scans</li>
          <li>Parkinson's prediction from voice measurements</li>
          <li>Diabetes and heart-disease prediction from tabular records</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="skills">
          Same skills as <ProjectLinks orders={[5, 6, 7]} /> (image classification) and
          <ProjectLinks orders={[1]} /> (tabular ML).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="domain-card">
        <h3>Marketing and retail</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Customer churn prediction</li>
          <li>Customer segmentation with clustering</li>
          <li>Customer lifetime value prediction</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="skills">
          Same skills as <ProjectLinks orders={[1]} /> (tabular classification) and
          <ProjectLinks orders={[4]} /> (clustering).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="domain-card">
        <h3>Sports, and other lanes</h3>
        <p>Named briefly so you know they exist: match-outcome prediction, player-performance models.</p>
        <p class="skills">Same underlying skills as everything above.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="closing">
      Finance is the lane this site teaches to depth. The others show the shape of the work and a real project to
      start on, not a full curriculum. Every non-finance example maps back to a function skill the track already
      teaches: this page is a different lens on the same 12 projects, not separate content.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .domains {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 5vw 120px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.2vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    color: var(--color-heading);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 48px;
  }
  .lede strong {
    color: var(--color-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .finance-lane {
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--lane-color) 30%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lane-color) 6%, transparent);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 28px 30px 30px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .lane-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--lane-color);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .finance-lane h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 26px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .finance-lane p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .domain-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .domain-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 24px 24px 26px;
  }
  .domain-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 19px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .domain-card ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .domain-card li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .domain-card p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .domain-card .skills {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .closing {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
